schema: "0.4"
id: npl-brutalist-08-mcp-api-keys-setup
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — MCP API Keys & Setup: a self-service hub for minting and managing
# MCP API keys, generating the `claude mcp add` setup command, and exploring the tool
# catalog exposed by a user's keys; surfaces key-lifecycle security states.
# Theme tenets: hard-grid table density, zero radius, full-strength borders + 1px grid,
# flat electric accents used as safety signal, hard-offset block shadow as only depth.
# Palette: vermilion #ff2d00, ultramarine #1500ff, hazard-yellow #ffe600, green #00c853,
# white #ffffff, black #000000, surface-alt #f2f2f2.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    security-grade settings hub inside a developer console, in a NEO-BRUTALIST register:
    dense, structural, shown as machinery. Color is used as safety signal (hazard
    palette), never decoration. Flat fills only — no gradient, glow, blur, or soft
    shadow; the only depth cue is a hard-offset SOLID block shadow with zero blur.
    Geometric grotesk (Space Grotesk) UPPERCASE 700 headings; Space Mono for keys,
    commands, table data, and schemas. No serif. Zero corner radius. Borders and table
    grid lines are load-bearing, always at full strength.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the MCP API KEYS & SETUP screen of NoizuPromptLingo
    — a self-service hub for minting and managing MCP API keys, generating the setup
    command, and exploring the tool catalog exposed by a user's keys — rendered as raw,
    high-voltage machinery.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (on a pure white canvas, a hard 12-column grid, regions separated by
    2px solid black rules): a top page header, a left-dominant API KEY TABLE + SETUP
    COMMAND stack, and a right TOOL CATALOG + TOOL DEFINITION column.

    PAGE HEADER: an uppercase grotesk 700 title "MCP API KEYS" and a solid vermilion
    "MINT KEY" button — rectangular, 2px black border, black uppercase mono label,
    hard-offset black block shadow with zero blur.

    API KEY LIST TABLE (dominant, dense): a hard-bordered table with 1px solid black grid
    lines on every cell, zero radius, uppercase mono column headers — NAME, STATUS,
    CREATED, LAST USED, ACTIONS. Rows of mono data; a KEY SECURITY STATUS BADGE per row
    rendered as a hard-bordered rectangular tag: an "ACTIVE" row with a solid electric-green
    badge (black text), a "REVOKED" row with a solid vermilion badge (white text), an
    "EXPIRED JWT" row with a solid hazard-yellow badge (black text) plus a bordered
    "REISSUE" action. One newly-minted key shown once as a bordered mono secret string with
    a "COPY" button.

    SETUP COMMAND GENERATOR (below the table): a wide bordered mono code block on a
    light-gray surface showing the "claude mcp add ..." command with the key embedded, a
    hard-offset black block shadow, and a bordered "COPY COMMAND" button.

    RIGHT TOOL CATALOG EXPLORER: a bordered search input (uppercase mono label "SEARCH
    TOOLS" above it) and a vertical list of hard-bordered tool rows in mono (tool name plus
    a short descriptor); the selected row is a full inverted block (solid black, white
    text). Below it a TOOL DEFINITION PANEL — a bordered card showing the selected tool's
    schema as a mono block, with an ultramarine "VIEW HELP" link. A small REMOTE TUNNEL
    SETUP CARD at the bottom: a bordered block with a status dot and mono instructions.

    PALETTE & TYPE: pure white canvas, pure black ink and full-strength borders and grid
    lines, electric vermilion for the mint button and revoked badge, hazard yellow for the
    expired badge, electric green for the active badge, pure ultramarine for links and
    focus — each flat and whole at maximum saturation. Space Grotesk uppercase headings,
    Space Mono for keys, commands, table data, and schemas. No serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero radius; 1-2px solid black borders and 1px table grid lines at
    full strength; the only depth is a hard-offset solid block shadow (zero blur) on the
    mint button and the command block. No gradient, glow, blur, or soft shadow.

    MOOD: dense, raw, structural — a security-grade control surface shown as machinery.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, rounded corners, drop-shadow blur, soft shadow, gradient, neon glow, pastel colors, frosted glass"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the screen — page header with Mint Key, dense API key table with security status badges, setup command mono block, right tool catalog explorer + tool definition panel + remote tunnel card"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Brutalist language — zero radius, full-strength solid black borders and 1px table grid, flat hazard palette as safety signal (green/vermilion/yellow badges) + ultramarine links/focus, hard-offset block shadow (zero blur), Space Grotesk uppercase + Space Mono, no serif, no gradient/glow/soft shadow"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Legible table-dense hierarchy on a hard grid, clear security states, plausible real security settings tool"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible mono keys/commands, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "rounded corners, soft/blurred drop shadow, gradient, glow, or frosted glass present"

tags: [npl-brutalist, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, api-keys, settings]
